<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent liftings fall sharply in week.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent liftings fall sharply in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent crude from the Sullom Voe terminal in the Shetland Islands fell by 244,243 tonnes to 432,188 tonnes in the week ending September 10, according to data published by the Shetland Islands Council.</p>
<p>All of the Brent went to refineries in Britain and northwest Europe and none went transatlantic.</p>
<p>Below is a list of loadings:</p>
<p> DATE    VESSEL		   DESTINATION	 CARGO (TONNES)</p>
<p> 4/9     Alandia Nord	    Hamburg	    69,301</p>
<p> 4/9     Alandia Fox	     Hamburg	    69,106</p>
<p> DATE    VESSEL		   DESTINATION	 CARGO (TONNES)</p>
<p> 5/9     Alandia Pearl	   Tranmere	   69,039</p>
<p> 6/9     Sunetta		   Tranmere	   76,288</p>
<p> 6/9     Centaur		   Milford Haven    69,202</p>
<p> 8/9     Alandia Pearl	   Gdansk	     79,252</p>
<p> WK ENDING U.K.     NWE	AMERICAS  MED     OTHER    TOTAL</p>
